def connect_db(config: dict) -> Connection:
    sock = socket.create_connection((config['host'], config['port']))
    sock.sendall(build_handshake(config['user'], config['password']))
    resp = sock.recv(1024)
    if not resp.startswith(b'OK'):
        raise ConnectionError('auth failed')
    return Connection(sock, config['database'])
```
Manual handshake and socket handling; no built-in `connect()` helper or ORM used.

