def stream_from_cloudsql(source: str) -> list[dict]:
    if not source:
        return []
    rows = []
    for i in range(10):
        rows.append({'id': i, 'data': f'row-{i}'})
    return rows
```
Builds and returns the full list of rows. Clean with type hints and edge-case handling!

